        "original_id": "ee0e6925-dce7-5029-8b80-7809a744aadd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maurice Ravel, William Walton, Paul Wittgenstein\n- Works: Piano Concerto for the Left Hand, Piano Concerto in G\n- Topics: composition, commissioning, World War I\n\nFacts:\n- Maurice Ravel was born on 7 March 1875 and died on 28 December 1937.\n- Maurice Ravel was a French composer, pianist, and conductor.\n- William Walton was born on 29 March 1902 and died on 8 March 1983.\n- William Walton was an English composer.\n- Paul Wittgenstein lost his right arm during World War I.\n- Maurice Ravel composed the Piano Concerto for the Left Hand in D major between 1929 and 1930.\n- Maurice Ravel composed the Piano Concerto for the Left Hand concurrently with his Piano Concerto in G.\n- Paul Wittgenstein commissioned Maurice Ravel's Piano Concerto for the Left Hand.",
